{
 "name": "Citadel Rush",
 "menuBackgroundImage": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bwellsean/citadel-rush-arena/main/images/banner.webp?v=2",
 "cardRotation": 90,
 "customHelp": "CITADEL RUSH quick reference\nBoard: 5 lanes (A-E) x 6 rows, shown the same way on both screens. Player 1 (the host, first seat) owns rows 1 to 3 at the bottom and moves up. Player 2 owns rows 4 to 6 at the top and moves down. Each Citadel sits beyond its owner's back row (row 1 for Player 1, row 6 for Player 2). Bring the enemy Citadel from 15 to 0 to win; track your own Citadel Health on your counter.\nHalcyte: you start with 6 in your supply. Turn 1 you have 1 (second player: 2), then 1 more each turn, max 6. At the start of your turn drag 1 from the supply to Available. Tap a Halcyte to spend it; they untap each turn.\nTurn: Draw 1. Main phase: deploy up to 1 Runner on an empty square of your back row, play any Traps, Upgrades and Protocols you can pay for, Infuse (1 Halcyte: +1 ATK this turn, max 2 per Runner), Citadel Strike (2 Halcyte: 3 damage to an enemy Runner in your back row, once per turn), and make up to 2 moves with different Runners (first move is required if possible). Free sidestep if a Runner is directly ahead. Attack phase: each Runner may attack once.\nTraps: play face down on an empty square in your half. Upgrades: drop onto your Runner (max 1).\nRunner Health: a hit of 2+ below the current Lethal drops 1 step; a hit at or above Lethal defeats it; 0 or 1 glances. Mark steps with the Wounded, Critical and Last Stand tokens (drag from the token bar onto the card). Only survivors hit back.\nDeck: 40 cards, 1 faction, at least 12 Runners, up to 3 copies, 1 Champion, at most 2 Legendary cards. The deck builder checks size and copies; check Champions, Legendaries and the 12-Runner minimum yourself.\nFull rules: https://claude.ai/artifact/SdixphB2RvUK1PvQtYAVz9",
